      "writtenOn": "2024-10-03T23:06:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "typec_set_input_current_limit and pd_set_input_current_limit just report available power to the charge manager. The charge manager runs in a HOOK thread and picks the port/supplier which can provide the highest power.\n\nWhen selecting the best supplier, the charge manager prefers PD to Type-C. However, it doesn\u0027t consider suppliers with current \u003d\u003d 0mA. So, I think that\u0027s why Type-C\u0027s current limit is effective.\n\nYou might as well call pd_set_input_current_limit with 1mA instead of 0 to verify the behavior.",
      "parentUuid": "c827ed6f_f230d1b1",
      "revId": "fdbd5e867e12e4fe6d5964b7905c54d9bfe60c26",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
